# Admit one phrase for a fixed future tick on this attachment's track.
# The scheduler snapshots KJ_TRACK, KJ_TICK, KJ_PHRASE_BEATS, KJ_TEMPO,
# KJ_PHRASE and KJ_HEARD before starting this lifecycle. A late script cannot
# move its target forward. Missed or invalid output uses the last good phrase.
# In 4/4, each quarter-note beat contributes one fourth of a bar.
set -e
bars=$(( KJ_PHRASE_BEATS / 4 ))
target=$(( KJ_TICK + KJ_PHRASE_BEATS ))
kj drive --track "$KJ_TRACK" --score-at "$target" --fallback last-good --prompt "Commit at tick $target. Transport: tick $KJ_TICK, phrase $KJ_PHRASE, $KJ_TEMPO BPM, 4/4 in C. Recently played (oldest→newest JSON): $KJ_HEARD. Play the NEXT phrase, continuing seamlessly from what you just played. Write exactly $KJ_PHRASE_BEATS quarter notes — ONE note per beat, 4 notes per bar, a barline | every 4 notes, $bars bars total — so the line is continuous with no gap. CRITICAL: with L:1/4 a bare note letter is exactly one beat (a quarter note); do NOT add duration numbers (no C2, no C/2) and do NOT pack multiple notes into a beat. Low register — use commas (C, G, A,). Output ONE complete ABC tune: X:1, then T:bass, M:4/4, L:1/4, K:C, then the body. Raw ABC only — no prose, no code fences."
